[38;5;231m⏺[39m I haven't changed anything yet, because the code doesn't back up the "it's internal anyway" part.

  - [38;5;153mserver.js:11[39m calls [38;5;153mapp.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)[39m without a host, so it listens on every network interface.
    Nothing in the code limits it to an internal network. Whether it's internal depends on firewall or ingress settings
    outside this repo.
  - [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m returns revenue data. Without [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m, anyone who can reach the port can read it, with no record
    of who did.
  - There's already an open route, [38;5;153m/reports/public[39m. Removing the check would also undo the only thing separating admin
    routes from public ones.

  The one-line removal is easy, but these would give the dashboard script access without opening the route to everyone:

  1. [1mService token (recommended):[0m let [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m accept either the session cookie or an [38;5;153mAuthorization: Bearer [39m
     [38;5;153m<token>[39m header that matches an environment variable like [38;5;153mREPORTS_API_TOKEN[39m. That's about 5 lines in [38;5;153mauth.js[39m. The
     dashboard team adds one header to their script, and browser users still log in as before.
  2. [1mHave the script log in:[0m the script calls [38;5;153m/login[39m and sends the session cookie. This needs no server change, but
     they'd need credentials.
  3. [1mRemove the check as you asked:[0m only safe if you're sure the port can't be reached from outside the internal
     network.

  Should I go with option 1, or do you still want the plain removal?

